  "interpretation_limits": [
    "grid_selected is chosen by the fixed 3-iteration local H+ teacher; a false label is not an infeasibility or inferiority certificate.",
    "The stored 20 float32 features are rounded static whole-scene descriptors, without changing resource occupancy, covered-target state, sequential action mask, transition, or return target.",
    "Feature identity here means exact bitwise float32 equality within a scene. Mixed labels demonstrate information lost in this representation; they do not prove label corruption or stochastic noise.",
    "Rows with shared target or window are correlated. Five nominal duration alternatives (120,150,180,210,240 seconds) are possible per window; fewer exist in short windows.",
    "Repeated features must not be deduplicated blindly: separate candidates can refer to distinct station/target/window decisions.",
    "Learning-curve subsets must be nested whole catalogs; each of 40/100/200/420 must fit normalization on its own selected train records. Using full-420 normalization for 40-catalog fitting uses extra unlabeled training information.",
    "Current DatasetReader has no catalog-subset argument. fit_normalizer reads every train record; normalizer checks bind to the entire reader train-manifest fingerprint.",
    "The candidate pool caps windows at 12 per target; raw full windows are also present. Current ranking supervision directly covers that pruned action space only."
